description:
Design a power-on reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal based on the presence of power and a clock signal. When power is supplied, a counter increments until it reaches a predefined limit (rst_time), at which point the reset output is asserted high. The circuit will hold the reset signal high for a brief duration determined by rst_time, ensuring that the system initializes properly after power-up. If power is lost, the reset signal is deasserted immediately.
module top_module(
  input power,
  input clk,
  output reset
);

code:
module top_module(
  input power,
  input clk,
  output reset
);parameter rst_time = 10; // length of time the reset signal should be asserted

reg [31:0] rst_counter;
reg reset_reg;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (power) begin
    rst_counter <= rst_counter + 1;
    if (rst_counter >= rst_time) begin
      reset_reg <= 1'b1;
      rst_counter <= 0;
    end
  end else begin
    reset_reg <= 1'b0;
    rst_counter <= 0;
  end
end

assign reset = reset_reg;

endmodule

