Design a positive-edge triggered D flip-flop with asynchronous active-low reset functionality. The module captures the value of the input `d` on the rising edge of the `clk` signal, while the output `q` reflects this value after a delay of two time units. If the `rst_n` signal is low, the flip-flop resets the output `q` to low, regardless of the clock signal.
